@sign_treaty
view-if: marcher_in_government and foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"
on-arrival: kellogg_briand_signed = 1

Foreign Minister Yardley will sign the treaty, of course. The reaction is generally muted; both pacifists and militarists are skeptical about the efficacy of the treaty.

Additionally, during [+ foreign_minister +]'s trip to Vera, there has been success in bringing the <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> to consider withdrawing from the Exetar early and to agree to another review of our War Loans by foreign experts.

- @step_forward
- @not_enough

@step_forward
view-if: kellogg_briand_signed
title: The treaty is a step forward for peace.

Despite our misgivings about the treaty, it still represents a step forward for the cause of international peace.

@not_enough
view-if: kellogg_briand_signed
title: The treaty is not enough.

Despite the idealism behind the treaty, it is inadequate for its goal of preventing wars. There must be some enforcement mechanism, perhaps automatic trade sanctions, or an intervention force answerable to the assembled realms. As it stands, the compact and this treaty are toothless.